※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7000 LANG_COMPTIME_CANNOT

※ The same module as image-worked-out-when-named, and this program names
※ `never`, which reads the table that cannot be worked out.  Named, it is worked
※ out -- and what the compiler cannot do there it says, as it would have said it
※ of the table in the program's own file: what moved is when it is asked, and
※ nothing about what it answers.

let std := ⎕import("std")
let tables := ⎕import("tables")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if tables.never(): 0u6 else: 1u6
